[00:00.00] I was closed, mouth open, watching closely, nothing spoke.
[00:30.80] Beneath glass, the world hushed, is a dream still a dream, if you can't wake up.
[00:45.80] Brain fevered body limb, in altered states the truth is glimpse.
[00:56.80] Descending stairwells of the mind drenched in morphine and iodine.
[01:12.80] Linolium smooth to the stocking foot, corridors dark seeing what I could.
[01:23.80] High priest in white lab coats evangelize the disease as the antidote.
[01:33.80] Signs by day, prayers by night, belief now stretched, sausage tight.
[01:44.80] Born in the bag, a drip dried, then sewn up with a poison still inside.
[02:00.80] Condemned as sick, though healthy the weak are despised by the wealthy.
[02:11.80] Endlessly nudged to scrub their hands to bang their pots and beat their pans.
[02:21.80] Then driven idiotic with fear, while dissenters are herded, then smeared.
[02:32.80] Tyrannized by quizlings and shields to self-censor till the silence chills.
[02:48.80] Mandates from self-appointed elites growing more demonic by decree.
[02:58.80] Yet a veil is lifting for all to see this ice-cold grip of insanity.
[03:09.80] What will remain of these nameless people? What will we name their remaining evil?
[03:20.80] Beneath the light, the cars no shadow, the path is fraught, but the gate still narrow.
[03:39.80] Transcribed by ESO, translated by —
